 necesidad que pudo contratarse de una vez.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 64 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 1.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 35.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 17.6 to 81.3. December accounts for 0% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 4% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 57 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,521.78 euros, was awarded in October 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The fact that many contracts are just under the limit does not prove that any of them were improperly awarded. It could be due to market prices, budget constraints, or the need for multiple smaller contracts to meet specific requirements. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the details of contract [1] to see what services were purchased and the reason for the amount being just under the limit. Also, review the distribution of contracts across different awardees to ensure no single provider was used excessively. Look at the timing of the contracts to see if there's a pattern in when they were awarded.","origen_es":"plantilla","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["0zGiinE6Ldt70UvEyYJSGw%3D%3D","7H%2FFcolyGD%2BS81gZFETWmA%3D%3D","HQyaeupb58UaF6cS8TCh%2FA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}